        "original_id": "ecddd54d-c79b-5453-87e7-40d48c018132",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sierra de Guadarrama National Park, Doñana National Park, Spain, Andalusia, Huelva, Seville\n- Organizations: Spain's national parks system\n\nFacts:\n- Sierra de Guadarrama National Park is a national park in Spain.\n- Sierra de Guadarrama National Park covers nearly 34,000 hectares.\n- Sierra de Guadarrama National Park is the fifth largest park in Spain's national parks system.\n- Doñana National Park is a natural reserve in Andalusia in southern Spain.\n- Doñana National Park is located in the provinces of Huelva and Seville, with most of its territory in Huelva.",
